<title>FRANCE: France 2 state TV unions join October 17 strike.</title>
<headline>France 2 state TV unions join October 17 strike.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Labour unions at France 2 state television said on Friday they would strike on October 17, the day of a civil service strike which has already been joined by rail and power utility workers.</p>
<p>Strike notice was served by the CFDT, the country's largest and pro-Socialist union, as well as the Communist-led CGT and the CGC, a white-collar employees union.</p>
<p>The unions said in a statement they were calling a 24-hour stoppage to protest against the breaking up of media groups, the 1997 budget for the audio-visual sector and the privatisation of the SFP film and television production studios.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
